n" 13194139534436 17592186045417 true] [17592186421527 1078 #edb/ref 17592186421502 13194139534436 17592186045417 true] [17592186421527 1079 #uuid "fe4e956c-1b1f-5312-af0b-3bb85188fdbd" 13194139534436 17592186045417 true] [17592186421528 1068 #edb/ref 17592186421527 13194139534436 17592186045417 true] [17592186421528 1069 "q-74609" 13194139534436 17592186045417 true] [17592186421528 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534436 17592186045417 true] [17592186421528 1071 "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc$, $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨-1,4,3⟩$, $c=⟨2,-6,-4⟩$, and  $u=⟨3,-7,-4⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" 13194139534436 17592186045417 true] [17592186421528 1072 #uuid "5b9c3557-0777-5517-a4eb-de326b8ca141" 13194139534436 17592186045417 true] [17592186421528 1074 "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-s+2t=3 \\\\ 4s-6t=-7 \\\\ 3s-4t=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -6 & -7 \\\\ 3 & -4 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -4 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-s+2t=3 \\\\ 2t=5 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n2t=5\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-s+2t & =3 \\\\ -s+2(\\frac{5}{2}) & =3 \\\\ -s+5 & =3 \\\\ -s & =-2 \\\\ s & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=2,\\,t=\\frac{5}{2},$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=2b+\\frac{5}{2}c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=2\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}=5.$" 13194139534436 17592186045417 true] [17592186421529 1068 #edb/ref 17592186421523 13194139534436 17592186045417 true] [17592186421529 1069 "q-34653" 13194139534436 17592186045417 true] [17592186421529 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534436 17592186045417 true] [17592186421529 1071 "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534436 17592186045417 true] [17592186421529 1072 #uuid "9fca2b37-ca0d-5f9c-9cd0-c84b2660c1c8" 13194139534436 17592186045417 true] [17592186421529 1074 "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-5.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+4(-5)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=20.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20{a}_{1}+(-5){a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 20\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+(-5)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=20\\cdot (-5)=-100.$" 13194139534436 17592186045417 true] [17592186421530 1068 #edb/ref 17592186421525 13194139534436 17592186045417 true] [17592186421530 1069 "q-105215" 13194139534436 17592186045417 true] [17592186421530 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534436 17592186045417 true] [17592186421530 1071 "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534436 17592186045417 true] [17592186421530 1072 #uuid "c75c18ab-94b6-560b-bd47-66c76f099710" 13194139534436 17592186045417 true] [17592186421530 1074 "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe second row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=1,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $b$ does *not* lie in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$" 13194139534436 17592186045417 true] [17592186421531 1068 #edb/ref 17592186421526 13194139534436 17592186045417 true] [17592186421531 1069 "q-105242" 13194139534436 17592186045417 true] [17592186421531 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534436 17592186045417 true] [17592186421531 1071 "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 18 \\\\ 39\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534436 17592186045417 true] [17592186421531 1072 #uuid "cdba03e5-45ad-5856-b84f-f9bccefe0c86" 13194139534436 17592186045417 true] [17592186421531 1074 "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 18 \\\\ 39\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+7{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+18{x}_{2}=-6 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+39{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 18 & -6 \\\\ 5 & 39 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 39 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & k+15\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & k+15\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+19\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k+19.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k+19\\,⇒\\,k=-19.\n$$" 13194139534436 17592186045417 true] [17592186421532 1068 #edb/ref 17592186421524 13194139534436 17592186045417 true] [17592186421532 1069 "q-105241" 13194139534436 17592186045417 true] [17592186421532 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534436 17592186045417 true] [17592186421532 1071 "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534436 17592186045417 true] [17592186421532 1072 #uuid "f6e087fb-be43-5d06-8b0f-af7c87178067" 13194139534436 17592186045417 true] [17592186421532 1074 "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-8{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ -12{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -12 & -6 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -12 & -6 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -12 & -6 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k-9.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k-9\\,⇒\\,k=9.\n$$" 13194139534436 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-118b15fa-3742-5277-8c58-23aa4caecb92" 17592186421498 "answer-18da01e3-a753-5c12-b310-e49dbac1352a" 17592186421499 "answer-1a7a3f85-c316-5d92-9f90-b24c014d8770" 17592186421500 "answer-244d18d1-69c9-554a-801a-a1ee85e653f9" 17592186421501 "answer-31aa51c7-7bbf-539a-8251-ca7e5420f8e3" 17592186421502 "answer-32eb1479-5bf7-5b7a-b94f-51a07f1faf34" 17592186421503 "answer-3730de20-b24e-5f5e-a26c-d563eb7c0ee1" 17592186421504 "answer-404186fe-c6bf-5419-b373-a5941944a534" 17592186421505 "answer-43f2e466-d80e-55b3-9568-6896ede2a380" 17592186421506 "answer-49efebb4-5b44-54d8-a642-d7be1bed4e5c" 17592186421507 "answer-7216d5b9-15dc-5173-80f7-9cff9ed9a669" 17592186421508 "answer-8b2ff67d-5ecb-55cb-9c92-917e51071eb6" 17592186421509 "answer-8b330e4c-1039-5eb3-95e3-86ecad96d372" 17592186421510 "answer-8c1e9e25-575f-5bba-bb57-6864dc973a15" 17592186421511 "answer-94545aa5-65f2-555f-8c83-9dc00de7552e" 17592186421512 "answer-961a42eb-d51a-527b-8228-58478af36cd7" 17592186421513 "answer-a5aeef05-ac8e-5ffc-b5cd-7dab5e605fc9" 17592186421514 "answer-afae5c38-3c29-54c4-8923-744473be6095" 17